      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u explain what exactly the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? i'm looking at a contract for electronic components moving from korea to germany and need to be sure about the insurance and freight handover points.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for paying the costs and freight necessary to bring the goods to the named port of destination in Germany, but the risk of loss or damage to the goods transfers to the buyer once the goods are loaded onto the vessel at the port of shipment in Korea. The seller must also obtain marine insurance covering the goods during the main carriage, though the buyer bears the risk if the goods are damaged or lost before reaching the destination.\n\nIn your specific case with electronic components moving from Korea to Germany, the seller handles all export formalities, packaging, loading onto the ship, and the freight charges up to the German port. However, the moment the components are safely on board the vessel in Korea, the risk shifts to you, the buyer, meaning any theft, damage, or loss at sea is your responsibility, not the seller's. The seller's obligation to provide insurance is mandatory under CIF, but it is typically a minimum coverage policy, so you should verify the extent of the coverage to ensure it adequately protects your high-value electronic components.\n\nIt is worth noting that while the seller pays for the freight to the German port, they do not",
